cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ESTIF: Emergent Spacetime from Inward Flow — Flow-Derived Gravity, Horizon-Scale MOND Acceleration, and the Dark-Energy Null"
abstract: >-
  ESTIF v6.4.2 derives gravity from three geometric axioms about a 3D
  hypersurface carried through a 4D bulk: A1' (slices are even on average;
  matter sources local dents; where nothing sources a dent, exact evenness
  returns; the spatial average of curvature is identically zero at all epochs
  -- the registered falsifier Omega_k = 0, current 0.0007 +/- 0.0019), A2
  (everything moves through the bulk at universal speed c), and A3 (vacuum
  sources nothing).

  DERIVED GRAVITY (v6.3, carried forward): the axioms uniquely select the
  constraint (energy) sector of General Relativity in Painleve-Gullstrand
  gauge, forcing rho_eff = m'(r)/(4 pi r^2) -- mass continuity / Poisson in
  integrated form. Vacuum gives v^2 = 2GM/r uniquely and exact Schwarzschild;
  a uniform-density source returns rho0 exactly; Lorentzian signature and
  special-relativistic kinematics emerge from a Euclidean bulk plus the
  universal speed-c constraint. The gravitational coupling (geometric
  constraint scalar to 8*pi*G times energy density) is adopted from
  Einstein-Hilbert, not derived from below.

  PHASE 2 NULL (v6.4.0, RHAC-004): the entire residual dark-energy stress the
  axioms permit was computed under a pre-registered binding declaration and
  submitted unmodified. It is EMPTY: shape and rate forbidden (A1, A2); slosh
  zero (pure-divergence theorem); swirl forbidden free and, if sourced,
  negative and slaved (~10^11 below rho_Lambda). w = -1 exactly; Lambda enters
  as a bare imported constant, exactly as in LCDM. ESTIF does not derive dark
  energy, and it is proven these axioms cannot. The former "frozen eddy"
  reading of the constant is retracted. The pre-registered chi^2/N ~ 0.66
  thawing target stands as the bar any outside-the-axioms evolving-w proposal
  must beat under honest marginalization.

  AXIOM AMENDMENT A1 -> A1' (RHAC-005/006): strict A1 was proven to forbid
  the growing density mode (unique solution decaying; f(z=0.5) = -0.91 vs
  measured +0.76 -- structure could not form) and the free radiative sector
  (vs LIGO). A1' (even on average) restores GR-equivalent linear growth
  D+ = H * int da/(aH)^3 with f(z=0.5) = 0.7603 (DESI RSD-consistent), the
  gravitational-wave sector, and a container for the zeta = 1e-5 seed (value
  imported). All strict-A1 results survive as the exact-evenness limit; the
  Phase 2 null was re-audited under A1' across five sectors and stands.

  GW SECTOR DERIVED (RHAC-008, C-15): under A1'+A2 the world is a single
  Lorentzian geometry; A3 plus the empty residual sector forbid any second
  metric or field. TT waves and light share the null cone for arbitrary flow,
  so c_gw = c with no free parameter. GW170817 is passed structurally
  (predicted deviation exactly zero).

  a0 HORIZON DOCTRINE (RHAC-010): a0 is a horizon-scale acceleration,
  a0 ~ c*H (de Sitter surface gravity). Mass-independence, asymptotically
  constant rotation curves, the baryonic Tully-Fisher relation, and the
  correct magnitude follow from this alone. Language stating the sqrt(3)
  prefactor, or the full numerical a0 coefficient, is derived: retired. The
  scale of a0 is derived; the O(1) prefactor is open. The working form
  a0 = H0*c*x0/sqrt(3) = 1.179e-10 m/s^2 (1.72% from the MOND empirical
  value; 1.1920e-10 and 0.66% with the conditional bootstrap Omega_m) remains
  operational: validated against 87 quality-1 SPARC galaxies (RMS 15.6%),
  redshift constancy proved as an algebraic identity (H(z) cancels in the
  comoving frame), and robust across 3,600 H0/Omega_m combinations.

  GROWTH AND THE FOUR LOCKS (RHAC-007, v6.4.1): fronts 1-3 computed the
  growth history D+(z), f(z), sigma8(z), f*sigma8(z) (JWST verdict: honest
  null -- the too-big-too-early tension is inherited from LCDM, neither
  relieved nor worsened), the first-black-hole fold-back rule
  nu*sigma(M,0)*D(z) = delta_c (star and direct-collapse channels
  characterized; primordial channel closed under the zeta = 1e-5 passport),
  and the growth index gamma = 0.5455-0.5544 over z = 0-5 (pull -0.23 sigma
  from DESI) with the slip lock (Sigma, eta, mu) = (1,1,1) exact. FOUR-LOCK
  LEDGER separating ESTIF-Core from GR's extra freedoms: Omega_k = 0
  (registered falsifier), gamma ~ 0.55 with slip = 1, w = -1, c_gw = c. None
  of the four separates ESTIF-Core from LCDM at Omega_k = 0 at linear order;
  the distinguishing content lives off the linear sheet (nonlinear halos --
  the N-body wall).

  COSMOLOGY (Path One): the constant-Lambda limit ties LCDM on DESI DR2 at
  chi^2/N = 1.965 (13-bin pipeline; supersedes the earlier 1.92 figure). The
  Omega_tilt(z) apparatus remains retired from the cosmology claim; its local
  strong-field use is unaffected, but deviation-from-GR figures (EHT shadow,
  LISA delay) are conditional on the un-derived non-vacuum sector (C1).

  OMEGA_M STATUS (RHAC-009): principle P (Omega_m = R_H/r_p) is proven
  non-derivable as a law -- the equality holds only near a = 1 (the two
  quantities cross once, today; at high z Omega_m -> 1 while R_H/d_p -> 1/2),
  so it cannot follow from the time-symmetric axioms. P is a predictive
  postulate; the conditional bootstrap (unique root 0.31408 with radiation,
  inputs {H0, T_CMB, N_eff}; 0.96% from Planck, 0.53 sigma) stands as
  conditional on P, and the "Omega_m derived" claim is retired. Prior art:
  the causal-horizon Omega_m ~ 0.3 result is Gaztanaga's (peer-reviewed,
  2019-2023); no priority is asserted on Omega_m.

  v6.4.2 HOUSEKEEPING: tests/ restructured to scripts/docs/plots with all
  paths repaired; documentation consolidated to four living files
  (PROJECT.md, SCIENCE.md, RHAC.md, CHANGELOG.md). Reproduce the headline
  result: python3 tests/scripts/estif_task4_field_equation.py

