    year: 2026
    version: "6.3.2"
    notes: >-
      Previous version. Derived the gravity field equation from the flow
      axioms (mass continuity = Poisson, via Gauss-Codazzi), fixed the
      cosmology circularity, split the project into Path One (Core) and Path
      Two (Extended), and added the conditional Omega_m bootstrap under
      principle P. Superseded by v6.4.x: Phase 2 closed as an honorable null
      (w = -1 exactly; Lambda a bare imported constant), axiom A1 amended to
      A1' (restoring linear growth and the radiative sector; Omega_k = 0
      registered as the falsifier), c_gw = c derived (C-15), principle P
      proven non-derivable (RHAC-009), and the a0 horizon doctrine adopted
      (RHAC-010).
  - type: software
    title: "ESTIF v6.2 — a0 Redshift Constancy Proved, Parameter Independence, Letter Drafted"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Angelov"
        given-names: "Peter"
    year: 2026
    version: "6.2.0"
    notes: >-
      Derived a0 = H0*c*x0/sqrt(3), validated against 87 SPARC galaxies
      (RMS 15.6%), tested against DESI DR2 (Omega_tilt sector fails
      chi^2/N = 10.8), proved a0 redshift constancy and parameter
      independence. Superseded by v6.3, which derives the gravity field
      equation from the flow axioms.
  - type: software
    title: "ESTIF-FD v1.0 — Emergent Spacetime from Inward Flow (Original)"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Angelov"
        given-names: "Peter"
    year: 2024
    version: "1.0.0"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.17261725"
    notes: >-
      Original cosmology version — S(t) = exp(-int H dt) ruled out by
      supernova data. Concept retained, equation abandoned.
